they could never have imagined a reunion  as bittersweet as this  for a few minutes one ukrainian family  are together again at a bus station in  warsaw then it's goodbye  daughters katarina and alina fled from  kiev a few days ago but their parents  who were in cuba on holiday when the war  broke out are only passing through the  bus station now on their way back into  ukraine  i don't want to stay in the safety of  poland she says i want to go home  katarina makes the sign of the cross  towards her father  it's the most horrible thing she says  anything could happen  it could be the last time i see my  parents  people are being directed towards  transport to take them to other polish  cities and across europe  vladimir putin's war is scattering  refugees near and far this group have  just got off a bus from central ukraine  they're now waiting to be taken to spain  a country none of them have any  connection with but somewhere which has  offered to take them in  for now this boy seeks his mother's love  but when he's older he'll remember this  who made them flee across europe who  made their lives hell  martyr aged 15 is already angry  i won't be in ukraine i won't be in my  home i won't be with my friends i won't  be with my family i won't be with my dad  with my dog i won't be with my family  keira waits with her mother and her toy  pig to be called forward to get on a  coach to estonia  there's no father figure to carry her  heavy bag the men have stayed in ukraine  to fight  her mother says i just want the wall to  stop that's all i want  then we see a bus which will cross  europe on its way to the british seaside  town of bournemouth though visa  restrictions mean only ukrainians with  family will be allowed to stay on the  bus until its final destination  on board this woman and her children  heading to france struggled over broken  bridges under gunfire to escape from  urpin nikkiev  she says her husband was so afraid for  them he forced them to go  [Music]  it's so bizarrely incongruous to hear  background music piped around the coach  as she describes running for their life  met by friends this beautician arrived  from the city of sumi she says there was  no water food or electricity  putin is in his bunker she says  sarcastically he's fine and he's smiling  there are few smiling here  warsaw bus station a sad scene of  separation and despair  lisa holland sky news warsaw
 

